{"BlockedEmail.should_block? performs database writes (updating match_count and last_match_at) during validation, violating the principle that validation should be read-only and creating unnecessary write load": 0.5547164082527161, "Email lookup does not perform canonicalization (downcase, strip), meaning 'User@Example.com' and 'user@example.com' would be treated as different emails, potentially bypassing blocks": 0.8202900290489197, "rejectedEmails array grows unbounded and may accumulate duplicate entries if user retries with same email multiple times - should check if email exists before adding": 0.20019996166229248, "rejectedEmails array should be reset when modal is closed or successful submission occurs to prevent stale client-side state": 0.15476727485656738, "BlockedEmail stats are not captured for emails already blocked by domain whitelist/blacklist policies, which may result in incomplete telemetry": 0.1823251098394394}